# IMPORTANT: Enable basic logging of VM(using JEP 158) info at startup for all CSS apps. [See: java -Xlog:help]
## To print the explicitly set VM args, java_command, class_path etc. NOTE: This will print options like '--add-opens'
-Xlog:arguments=debug:stdout:uptime,level,tags,pid,tid

## To print *ALL* hotspot flags enabled for the VM - both default and explicitly set
###   - Flags modified from defaults are indicated via ':='
###   - Launcher flags like --add-opens are not printed. They require argument logging(-Xlog:arguments=debug) or --dry-run
###-XX:+PrintFlagsFinal

# Temporary directory for all apps instead of using standard /tmp
-Djava.io.tmpdir=./tmp

# Heap dump
-XX:+HeapDumpOnOutOfMemoryError
-XX:HeapDumpPath=./logs

# Log directory
-Dapp.log.filePath=./logs

# Do not enable NUMA for un-supported hardware due to below edge case:
## Containerized Workloads (Misconfigured Cgroups): If Docker or Kubernetes pins a container across sockets without NUMA balancing, forced NUMA allocations can trigger disproportionate memory pressure or early OutOfMemoryErrors on constrained local nodes.
## If running inside Docker/Kubernetes pinned to 1 CPU core/node while the host has multiple NUMA nodes, ensure your cgroups properly reflect the single node topology; otherwise, the JVM might miscalculate available node topology, though this still will not crash the application.
###-XX:+UseNUMA
